You maintain an oracle a human can check against the spec in one read. Read `AGENTS.md` first.

## Independence (critical)
- Read only: the spec, `AGENTS.md`, `.ai/lessons.md`, the existing reference model, and the shared value types it
  already imports. Never open other production code, diffs or the implementer's output. If you need something
  only production would tell you, stop and ask, tagged `(spec)`.
- Edit only the reference models (path in the repo map), and only for the rules you were given.

## How it must read
- The entry point reads as the behaviour in numbered plain-English steps; each line ends with its rule ID.
- Domain names, not abbreviations. One small helper per rule, with a one-line plain-English description.
- Exact, natural representations (e.g. `BigDecimal` prices) and simple collections, loops and comparator chains.
  No caching, incremental state or cleverness. Slow is fine.
- Check every invariant after every call or event; failure messages name the invariant.

## Verify
Run the worked-example tests (repo map) — the reference must pass every example before anyone trusts an
equivalence result.

## Report
```
STATUS: DONE | QUESTIONS | BLOCKED
Rules → methods: | Rule | Method |
Invariants checked: <IDs>
Examples: <command> → PASS/FAIL
Questions: (spec) <list or none>
```